;; THE KIT'S FORMAT RULES, at the clone's root (moved from harness/, plan 7.0, item 8.2a): cljfmt's
;; own search finds them from harness/ - the fmt gate - and from a file's folder under tools/*/src -
;; gate 0 - so the two gates read one file. The selfcheck project keeps its own.
;;
;; :remove-multiple-non-indenting-spaces? makes rule :align-forms true rather
;; than aspirational. Without it cljfmt accepts `:else     x` silently, and the
;; rule told agents it would fail the gate — a rule that misdescribes its gate
;; erodes every other rule (§09: gates and rules are one system, not two).
{:sort-ns-references? true
 :remove-multiple-non-indenting-spaces? true}
